      "name": "mn-chi-cache",
      "path": "mn-chi-cache/",
      "contentSource": {
        "kind": "family",
        "branch": "cat/qou/mn-chi-cache/",
        "keyFrom": "mn-chi-q-<engine-key>, where engine-key is the wheel-cache / trace-cache source key (git trees of crates/pyhecke-native and crates/hecke-engine)",
        "declaredIn": "storage"
      },
      "holdsGraph": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/mn-chi-cache"
      ],
      "description": "Exact values of `pyhecke_native.mn_chi_q(lambda, mu)`, the q-Murnaghan-Nakayama Hecke character table, stored so a sweep that needs a heavy table (n = 24, 27) computes each entry once. One orphan branch per engine source key; inside it, content-addressed JSONL shards of (lambda, mu) -> the producer's exact [q-degree, coefficient-string] pairs, never a float. Before 2026-11-22 this was the in-tree file computations/.derived-chi-mn-cache.json, keyed by (lambda, mu) alone, so an entry from one engine build was served to every later one. Read and written by computations/derived_chi_catalogue_mn_disk_cache.py through the shared layer (scripts/lib/branch-cache.sh, computations/_branch_cache.py); it restores by default but seeds origin only when QOU_MN_CHI_CACHE_PUSH=1. A dirty engine tree has no key and nothing is served from the store; loaded entries are re-checked against the live binary first. `mn-chi-cache/` is where a member is mounted; nothing is tracked there. The kind is `typologies/mn-chi-cache.json`.",
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/qou/directory/mn-chi-cache"
    }
  ]
}
